WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:06.221
Brooklyn arrived early for practice on Monday after school.

2
00:00:06.222 --> 00:00:13.636
Before she pushed through the gym door, she heard a ball bouncing on the court.

3
00:00:13.637 --> 00:00:18.467
Inside she saw just one player—Marv.

4
00:00:18.468 --> 00:00:29.445
The coach was dribbling a big brown ball instead of the usual orange one. He circled around and dribbled the ball between his legs.

5
00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:33.579
Then he threw it behind his head without looking at the basket.

6
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:35.860
Swoosh!

7
00:00:35.861 --> 00:00:42.857
Brooklyn clapped. "Great shot! What's with that old-school ball?"

8
00:00:42.858 --> 00:00:48.504
"When I played college hoops, we used this type of ball." Marv laughed.

9
00:00:48.505 --> 00:00:55.670
"Dribbling this thing is like dribbling a watermelon, but it's fun. Ready to set up for practice?"

10
00:00:55.671 --> 00:00:59.108
"Sure," said Brooklyn. "How's Coach?"

11
00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:02.258
"He's home from the hospital and trying to rest.

12
00:01:02.259 --> 00:01:05.425
But it won't be easy once the babies come home."

13
00:01:05.426 --> 00:01:10.074
Coach and his wife had their triplets now: two girls and one boy.

14
00:01:10.075 --> 00:01:16.580
Poor Coach had to rest for a few weeks on pillows. It wasn't his hip that had been injured.

15
00:01:16.581 --> 00:01:22.914
"I can't coach with a broken rear end," he'd told the team when they'd visited him at the hospital.

16
00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:26.387
"Marv will be in charge. Brooklyn will assist him."

17
00:01:26.388 --> 00:01:35.316
Brooklyn pulled a large binder from her backpack. "Marv, wait until you see these plays I collected!"

18
00:01:35.317 --> 00:01:38.090
"Let's wait until after warm-ups, Brooklyn."

19
00:01:38.091 --> 00:01:39.218
"But—"

20
00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:47.102
"Team time!" Jacey cried, entering the gym with some other Whales.

21
00:01:47.103 --> 00:01:50.555
"Fun time!" several players echoed.

22
00:01:50.556 --> 00:01:55.368
"Team time! Fun time!" was one of Coach Teagan's favorite sayings.

23
00:01:55.370 --> 00:02:00.795
He told the Whales to forget about friends and problems and everything else during practice.

24
00:02:00.796 --> 00:02:06.962
"Team time" meant it was time to do one thing: play basketball.

25
00:02:06.963 --> 00:02:14.532
Brooklyn opened the equipment bag and twenty basketballs rolled out.

26
00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:21.024
Then she scanned the court, taking attendance. Every Whales player, except Dirk, was on the court.

27
00:02:21.025 --> 00:02:27.936
She knew Dirk was mad about the big bruises under his eyes and Brooklyn's new job as assistant coach.

28
00:02:27.937 --> 00:02:31.599
But that didn't mean he could skip practice.

29
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.241
"Maybe Marv excused him," Brooklyn thought.

30
00:02:35.242 --> 00:02:45.755
During warm-ups Brooklyn tossed back balls that bounced off the court.

31
00:02:45.756 --> 00:02:51.754
She also took notes whenever she thought of anything that might help the team.

32
00:02:51.755 --> 00:02:59.501
As soon as Marv blew the whistle for a break, Brooklyn ran over to him.

33
00:02:59.502 --> 00:03:08.280
"I noticed a bunch of problems!" she burst out. "Stuart and Aaron are traveling with the ball. Jacey needs to tighten up her dribbling."

34
00:03:08.281 --> 00:03:15.797
"We'll work on those things," Marv murmured. He looked around the gym. "Dirk still isn't here?"

35
00:03:15.798 --> 00:03:20.960
Brooklyn shook her head. "I thought maybe you'd excused him from practice."

36
00:03:20.961 --> 00:03:25.441
"Nope. Please call him and report back to me."

37
00:03:25.442 --> 00:03:31.209
Brooklyn found Dirk's cell phone number and dialed it.

38
00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:36.785
"No answer," she told Marv a few minutes later. "I left a message for him."

39
00:03:36.786 --> 00:03:46.424
Marv sighed. "We need Dirk in practice to work on our plays. I'll see if Coach has a home number for him in the office."

40
00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:51.596
He blew the whistle again. "Take two more minutes, team."

41
00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:59.324
Brooklyn wrote down some more notes as Jacey jogged past to get her water bottle.

42
00:03:59.325 --> 00:04:03.006
"Hey, Brooklyn, are you doing homework?" Jacey called.

43
00:04:03.007 --> 00:04:09.328
"No, I'm keeping practice notes," Brooklyn answered. "I've already noticed some problems."

44
00:04:09.329 --> 00:04:14.210
She reached for Jacey's ball. "I have a tip for you, Jacey.

45
00:04:14.211 --> 00:04:18.156
You need to dribble closer to your body to protect the ball." Stuart

46
00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:31.384
dashed over and grabbed the ball from Brooklyn. "Stuart steals!" He ran to a net and scored. Brooklyn

47
00:04:31.385 --> 00:04:38.716
smiled. "Well, that illustrates my point: tighten up your dribbling or the ball will get stolen from you." Jacey

48
00:04:38.717 --> 00:04:42.872
frowned. "You're not our coach, Brooklyn." Just

49
00:04:42.873 --> 00:04:53.295
then the gym door swung open. Dirk entered and put down his gym bag. "Let's play ball!" "You're

50
00:04:53.296 --> 00:05:00.628
late," Brooklyn said. "Take three laps around the court. Remember Coach's rules for tardiness." "But

51
00:05:00.629 --> 00:05:08.286
Coach isn't here, is he?" Dirk pretended to look for him under his gym bag. "Coach?" Jacey

52
00:05:08.287 --> 00:05:13.181
laughed loudly. "Good one!" Brooklyn

53
00:05:13.182 --> 00:05:17.614
crossed her arms. "You know the rules, Dirk." Marv

54
00:05:17.615 --> 00:05:25.273
returned from the gym office. "I'll handle this, Brooklyn. Dirk, let's chat." Some

55
00:05:25.274 --> 00:05:36.682
other Whales began throwing passes. Brooklyn watched Marv nod as he listened to Dirk. A

56
00:05:36.683 --> 00:05:43.558
few minutes later, Dirk ran onto the court and grabbed a basketball. He

57
00:05:43.559 --> 00:05:53.994
tossed several long shots, swooshing the ball through the hoop each time. "Team,

58
00:05:53.995 --> 00:05:59.667
copy Dirk," Marv said. "Free throws. Do at least twenty each." While

59
00:05:59.668 --> 00:06:08.113
the Whales practiced, Brooklyn pulled some pages from her binder. The

60
00:06:08.114 --> 00:06:17.550
pages showed step-by-step instructions for Hip-Hop Delight, a play executed last year by the women's team at the University of Connecticut. It

61
00:06:17.551 --> 00:06:20.800
had won them a championship game. Brooklyn

62
00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:25.805
had numbered and sketched each step in the play. She

63
00:06:25.806 --> 00:06:31.788
pointed at one of the sketches for Marv. "Can we try this with our team?" Marv

64
00:06:31.789 --> 00:06:36.391
studied the play for a few minutes. "You think like a coach, kid! This

65
00:06:36.392 --> 00:06:41.543
Hip-Hop Delight play will definitely confuse opponents. Let's try it!" The

66
00:06:41.544 --> 00:06:46.200
two coaches joined the players under a net. Marv

67
00:06:46.201 --> 00:06:52.707
instructed each player where to stand to start the play. He gave a basketball to Dirk. "Toss

68
00:06:52.708 --> 00:06:57.926
the ball away from our net first, across your left hip. Pass it to Aaron. He'll

69
00:06:57.927 --> 00:07:02.605
dribble to midcourt to Jacey, passing the ball to her right side. This

70
00:07:02.606 --> 00:07:09.270
is a complicated play," Marv added, "but if it works, we'll score points. Right, Brooklyn?" "Right!"

71
00:07:09.271 --> 00:07:11.170
Marv

72
00:07:11.171 --> 00:07:15.296
blew his whistle. "Let's go!" Dirk

73
00:07:15.297 --> 00:07:26.092
dribbled. He turned, throwing the ball to Aaron, but Marv quickly blew his whistle again to stop practice. "Dirk,

74
00:07:26.093 --> 00:07:29.580
go the other way before passing the ball." After

75
00:07:29.581 --> 00:07:37.398
five tries Dirk stomped over to Marv. "This play makes no sense!" "Calm

76
00:07:37.399 --> 00:07:45.906
down," said Marv. "This is a smart play. With practice, we can make it work. Brooklyn, show him your sketch." Dirk's

77
00:07:45.907 --> 00:07:52.468
face turned red. " She planned this play? No wonder it doesn't work!"

78
00:07:52.469 --> 00:07:57.221
Brooklyn held up her sketches. "All you have to do—"

79
00:07:57.222 --> 00:08:04.974
"Girls can't coach guys, especially not you!" Dirk stormed out of the gym.

80
00:08:04.975 --> 00:08:08.522
Marv called after him. "Dirk! Stop!"

81
00:08:08.523 --> 00:08:13.563
"I know this play can work," Brooklyn said, looking at the rest of the team.

82
00:08:13.564 --> 00:08:18.552
Jacey frowned and shook her head. The other players were looking away.

83
00:08:18.553 --> 00:08:23.184
"Dirk will start Thursday's game on the bench," Marv announced.

84
00:08:23.185 --> 00:08:30.867
"Great," Jacey muttered sarcastically. "Will your big play work without our best player, Brooklyn?"

85
00:08:30.868 --> 00:08:37.357
"Enough!" Marv pointed sharply at Jacey. "You just earned a spot on the bench too!"

86
00:08:37.358 --> 00:08:44.770
Brooklyn looked down. "It always takes time for players to accept a new coach," she told herself.

87
00:08:44.771 --> 00:08:54.747
She just hoped it would happen before play-offs began.

